# The sample files under public/samples/ are deliberately small and mostly
# ASCII, so git's "is this binary?" heuristic (look for a NUL in the first 8k)
# guesses wrong and classifies them as text. With core.autocrlf=true that
# rewrites every LF to CRLF on checkout, which shifts the byte offsets a PDF's
# xref table points at — a fresh clone on Windows gets files that no longer
# open. Say it explicitly instead of relying on the guess.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.tif   binary
*.tiff  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
